[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466833454","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2466833454","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2466833454,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TCOQu","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-10T18:16:06Z","updated_at":"2024-11-10T18:16:06Z","body":"Reproduced on a M2 Mac as far back as 4.4-dev1. Turning off the Metal backend removes the artifacts\r\n\r\nCC @stuartcarnie \r\n\r\n<img width=\"737\" alt=\"Screenshot 2024-11-10 at 9 58 01 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7adc42aa-c66b-4117-b4aa-e1ad0fa5fa29\">\r\n\r\nThe artifacts go away if you disable world_triplanar, then toggle triplanar and enable world_triplanar in the material, but then come back if you click on the node in the scenetree. So I suspect there is some leaking state going on.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466833454/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466975374","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2466975374","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2466975374,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TCw6O","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-10T22:57:52Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T00:05:01Z","body":"> So I suspect there is some leaking state going on.\r\n\r\n@clayjohn can you elaborate on \"some leaking state\" and what that might be – what should I be looking for?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2466975374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2467110975","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2467110975","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2467110975,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TDSA_","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T02:28:44Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T02:28:44Z","body":"@stuartcarnie I'm not sure exactly. It would be if anything is set globally instead of per command. For example, Vulkan as the ability to set certain state (like the viewport rect) dynamically. If you forget to reset that state it can leak into other operations. \r\n\r\nThis artifact to me looks like its reading from un-initialized memory in the fragment shader. So a very rough guess would be something like a sampler state is leaking for one of the textures. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2467110975/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469139280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2469139280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2469139280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TLBNQ","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T21:59:12Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T21:59:12Z","body":"@clayjohn curiously, if I enable the **Grow** option, the issue goes away. Seems like it might be an issue with the layout of the `MaterialUniforms`, which is affected by that change.\r\n\r\nWithout `grow` enabled, the generated struct in the Metal source looks like this:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nstruct MaterialUniforms\r\n{\r\n\tfloat4 m_albedo;\r\n\tfloat m_point_size;\r\n\tfloat m_roughness;\r\n\tfloat4 m_metallic_texture_channel;\r\n\tfloat m_specular;\r\n\tfloat m_metallic;\r\n\tfloat m_uv1_blend_sharpness;\r\n\tfloat3 m_uv1_scale;\r\n\tfloat3 m_uv1_offset;\r\n\tfloat3 m_uv2_scale;\r\n\tfloat3 m_uv2_offset;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nwith grow:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nstruct MaterialUniforms\r\n{\r\n    float4 m_albedo;\r\n    float m_grow;\r\n    float m_point_size;\r\n    float m_roughness;\r\n    float4 m_metallic_texture_channel;\r\n    float m_specular;\r\n    float m_metallic;\r\n    float m_uv1_blend_sharpness;\r\n    float3 m_uv1_scale;\r\n    float3 m_uv1_offset;\r\n    float3 m_uv2_scale;\r\n    float3 m_uv2_offset;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469139280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469391328","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2469391328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2469391328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TL-vg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T01:16:49Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T01:16:49Z","body":"@stuartcarnie Oh! Its a struct padding issue. Every graphics API handles struct padding slightly differently. Universally 3 floats in a row will add an extra float of padding. But two floats are handled differently, some will pad that to 4, but others won't pad when its only 2. \r\n\r\nWe are using SPIRV-Cross right? It might have some options to force a particular padding. But its probably just best for us to  add padding in the shader compiler","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469391328/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469662763","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2469662763","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2469662763,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TNBAr","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T05:47:59Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T05:47:59Z","body":"@clayjohn I had a suspicion it might be that. I'll dig a bit deeper into padding.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469662763/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471465921","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2471465921","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2471465921,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TT5PB","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T20:03:32Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T20:03:44Z","body":"@clayjohn I'm curious how the `MaterialUniforms`, which is generated at runtime, is valid, given size and alignment rules for Vulkan appear to be the same as Metal.\r\n\r\nThis is the generated version that I see (with offset / size as comment):\r\n\r\n```glsl\r\nstruct MaterialUniforms\r\n{\r\n    float4 m_albedo;                    //   0 / 16\r\n    float m_point_size;                 //  16 /  4\r\n    float m_roughness;                  //  20 /  4\r\n    float4 m_metallic_texture_channel;  //  24 / 16\r\n    float m_specular;                   //  40 /  4\r\n    float m_metallic;                   //  44 /  4\r\n    float m_uv1_blend_sharpness;        //  48 /  4\r\n    float3 m_uv1_scale;                 //  52 / 16\r\n    float3 m_uv1_offset;                //  68 / 16\r\n    float3 m_uv2_scale;                 //  84 / 16\r\n    float3 m_uv2_offset;                // 100 / 16\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nvs what I would expect is valid, based on Vulkan and Metal rules:\r\n\r\n```glsl\r\nstruct MaterialUniforms\r\n{\r\n    float4 m_albedo;                    //   0 / 16\r\n    float m_point_size;                 //  16 /  4\r\n    float m_roughness;                  //  20 /  4\r\n    float2 pad1;                        //  24 /  8\r\n    float4 m_metallic_texture_channel;  //  32 / 16\r\n    float m_specular;                   //  48 /  4\r\n    float m_metallic;                   //  52 /  4\r\n    float m_uv1_blend_sharpness;        //  56 /  4\r\n    float pad2;                         //  60 /  4\r\n    float3 m_uv1_scale;                 //  64 / 16\r\n    float3 m_uv1_offset;                //  80 / 16\r\n    float3 m_uv2_scale;                 //  96 / 16\r\n    float3 m_uv2_offset;                // 112 / 16\r\n};\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471465921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471536125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2471536125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2471536125,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TUKX9","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T20:38:31Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T20:38:31Z","body":"I can confirm that when I write the struct using Apple `simd` types, it matches Metal's padding rules:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nstruct MaterialUniforms\r\n{\r\n\tsimd_float4 m_albedo;                    //   0 / 16\r\n\tfloat m_point_size;                      //  16 /  4\r\n\tfloat m_roughness;                       //  20 /  4 (+ 8 bytes padding)\r\n\tsimd_float4 m_metallic_texture_channel;  //  32 / 16\r\n\tfloat m_specular;                        //  48 /  4\r\n\tfloat m_metallic;                        //  52 /  4\r\n\tfloat m_uv1_blend_sharpness;             //  56 /  4 (+ 4 bytes padding)\r\n\tsimd_float3 m_uv1_scale;                 //  64 / 16\r\n\tsimd_float3 m_uv1_offset;                //  80 / 16\r\n\tsimd_float3 m_uv2_scale;                 //  96 / 16\r\n\tsimd_float3 m_uv2_offset;                // 112 / 16\r\n};\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471536125/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471662425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2471662425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2471662425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TUpNZ","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-12T21:54:53Z","updated_at":"2024-11-12T21:54:53Z","body":"I found this issue https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Cross/issues/1572#issuecomment-749241274\r\n\r\nWe need manual padding to handle this, as the Metal driver uses argument buffers, which contain embedded structs for the descriptor sets.\r\n\r\nI'm going to try the latest version of MoltenVK and enable argument buffers to see if the same problem exists.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2471662425/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479767458","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99029#issuecomment-2479767458","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99029","id":2479767458,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tzj-i","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T19:23:58Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T19:23:58Z","body":"For reference, Godot and Metal agreed on the struct layout – it was an unrelated issue per #99261","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479767458/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]